  "Chelsea put on a show at Stamford Bridge and beat West Ham 2-0. Nicolas Jackson had the first big chances early, at 6' and 13', and Moisés Caicedo came close at 8'. The home side kept on coming, but West Ham held firm for a long time. Their best moment came at 71', when Tomás Soucek had a big chance, but Chelsea's defence stood tall.",
